      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <p>HAVE YOU TRIED WHITE COB Self=Raising Flour? IF NOT, WHY NOT? Wholesale by</p>
        <p>J. Povey &amp; Son Ltd. BRIDGE STREET, \\ARRINGTON.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0003" n="art0003">
        <p>QT. ANN'S PARISH C.IIIIRCH, To-MORROW (SUNDAY), DEC. 31st. SPECIAL PREACHERS: 10.30 earl.: The LORD BISHOP OF LIVERPOOL. 2.30 p.m.: THE VICAR. - 0.30 p.m.: The Rev. J. T. OWEN, Cntate of Winwick. Special Services Of Prayer. Thanksgiving and Resolve.</p>
        <p>MEE Archbishops ps.liaving re- quested the Clergy. of the Church of Eng- land to observe TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), the 31st instant, as a DAY OF THANKSGIVING, INTERCESSION and PRAYER in Connection with the War, A SERVICE will be held at the Parish Church at 3 p.m., at which the Mayor and Corporation and other representatives of Civic life will attend. It is hoped that as many as possible of the people of Warrington will be present. PETER PEACOCK, Mayor. FREDERIC W. WILLIS, Rector and Mayor's Chaplain.</p>
        <p>B ANK HOLIDAY. By Royal Proclamation all Banks WILL BE CLOSEL; on MONDAY NEXT (NEW YEAR'S DAY).</p>
        <p>XTOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the part- nership- heretofore subsisting between us, the undersigned, WILLIAM GARNETT and JAMES GA.RNETT, carrying on business as Farmers at the Pouch and Hook Farm, Grappenhall, in the County of Chester, was on the 18th day of Decem- ber, 1916, DISSOLVED by mutual consent. All debts due to and owing by the late firm will be received and paid respectively by the said JAMES GARNETT, who for the future will carry on the business on his own account in his own name. Dated this Twenty-second day of December, 1916. WILLIAM GARNETT, JAMES GARNETT.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON</p>
        <p>MASTER BAKERS'</p>
        <p>ASSOCIATION</p>
        <p>NATIONAL BREAD.</p>
        <p>To effect an economy in labour the above Bread will be mannfacture.d in</p>
        <p>TINS &amp; COBS ONLY.</p>
        <p>THE PRICE BEING 10D. PER 4. LOAF.</p>
        <p>OLYMPI A, LIVERPOOL. THE GREAT CIRCUS.</p>
        <p>ENORMOUS SUCCESS: TWO PERFORMANCES DAILY (Saturday included) at 2 and 7.</p>
        <p>Special Attractions: THE FULL BAND OF H.M. GRENADIER</p>
        <p>üblie Notices. _ „ f, '• ktl? and Bisho</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0004" n="art0004">
        <head>GUARDS</head>
        <p>GUARDS</p>
        <p>Special prices for children. Seats booked by post, telegram, or 'phone 365 Anfield, Liverpool.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0005" n="art0005">
        <p>IVARRINGTON E.I. CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETY, LIMITED.</p>
        <p>EDUCATION COMMITTEE. A GRAND CONCERT</p>
        <p>will be given in the</p>
        <p>CO-OPERATIVE HALL, CAIRO-STREET,</p>
        <p>THURSDAY NEXT. JANUARY 4th</p>
        <p>MISS BELLA BAILLIE, MADAM GERTRUDE BROOKS; Mr. HARRY PASHLEY, and the cele- brated Humorist. Mr. ARTHUR GUILDFORD.</p>
        <p>Speaker: Mr. W. H. SHERBTJRN. Chair to be taken at 7.30 by Mr. W. WRIGHT. CHILDREN NOT ADMITTED.</p>
        <p>CIOUNTY BOROUGH OP WARRINGTON. DEFENCE OF THE REALM. CULTIVATION OF LAND ORDER. The -Small Holdings and, Allotments Com- mittee invite TENDERS for the supply of the under-mentioned goods:— . GARDEN SPADES, at per dozen. GARDEN FORKS, at per dozen. GARDEN RAKES, at per dozen. • CatR.DEN DUTCH HOES, at per dozen. GARDEN BARROWS, at each. Horse, Cow, or Pig MANURE, at per load delivered within the Borough. POTATO SETS (name and where grown to be stated), at per cwt. or bushel. Tender o to be addressed_to the Chairman of the Small Holdings and Allotments Committee, Town Clerk's Office, Warrington, and to be de- livered. with komplett of 'lmplements, at the Town Hall on or'before January 6th. J. LYON WHITTLE, Town Clerk.</p>
      </div>
