      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0015" n="art0015">
        <p>SATURDAY, DECEMBER 30, 1916.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0016" n="art0016">
        <head>MILLER 82 Co.</head>
        <p>MILLER 82 Co.</p>
        <p>10, Sankey St., Warrington. TELEPHONE 386.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0017" n="art0017">
        <head>NEW YEAR'S GIFTS</head>
        <p>NEW YEAR'S GIFTS</p>
        <p>• A imos 111, • 50, Horsentarket Street, NEXT DOOR TO MR. HALLETT'S, THE JEWELLER. WE DESIRE to sincerely thank all those Mothers and Babies who so kindly gave us their Christmas trade ; to wish them all good health and prosperity . for the coming year; and to assure them that we shall continue to supply their wants with the same High-class goOds at the same very moderate prices. 1 I Cb ' , •ft• , 50, Horsemarket Street, NEXT DOOR TO MR. HALLETT'S, THE JEWELLER.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0018" n="art0018">
        <p>NEW TERM • Beginners' Classes- in all Depts. of the College will COMMENCE on the r , ??,;!, • ,• r . r and the enrolling period will continue to 3rd Feb. PLEASE NOTE-NEW PUPILS ARE ACCEPTED AND OAN COMMENCE ON ANY DAi THROUGHOUT THE YEAR. BUT IT IS ADVANTAGEOUS TO ENROL AT THE COMMENOEMENT OF I A.TERM. FIVE GOOD REASONS for the ever-increasing Popularity and Growth of WOOD'S COLLEGE:- 1. BECAUSE WOOD'S COLLEGE IS THE Longest-established and most influential Business College in WARRINGTON AND DISTRICT. 2. BECAUSE WOOD'S COLLEGE has FINE Premises, CENTRALLY SITUATED, PERFECT EQUIPMENT ON A LIBERAL SCALE. Every Model of MODERN STANDARD typewriter. 3. BECAUSE WOOD'S COLLEGE SPECIALISES AND EXCELS in Teaching SHORTHAND dr, TYPEWRITING —in the minimum practicable TIME. 4. BECAUSE WOOD'S COLLEGE has secured 106 DIRECT appointments since 3rd January, 1916, in Warrington and District. Proofs can be inspected. 5. BECAUSE WOOD'S COLLEGE CONDUCTS PERIODICAL PUBLIC EXAMINATIONS BY RECOGNISED DOMES, UNDER the direct super- vision of disinterested LOCAL COMMITTEES. UPWARDS OF 550 CERTIFICATES SECURED SINCE 3RD JANUARY, 1916. --siorrer• Principal &amp; Proprietor—F. WILSON WOOD, F 1.111. Private address (for interviewing prospective students on the follow- ing dates: December 23rd, 27th, 28th..29th, 30th, 1910; also January 2nd, 1917) :—IIBATHFIELD VILLAS, FAIRFIBLD-ROAD, STOCKTON HEATH. Send to-day for new Booklet: "The Centre for Business Training"; or for the Complete Illustrated "Prospectus Guide." Call personally on the 3rd January, 1917, and we will show you over the Institution. 15, BRIDGE STREET WARRINGTON.</p>
      </div>
