        <p>TRAINS "SCRATCHED "—continued.</p>
        <p>will make use of that at Dareshnry. Happily, there has not been extensive interference with the service to and from that station, though there will be ohanges. Among the trains which are to cease running is the 2.6. Business people living Frodsham way may find th"alteration of the 9in convenient, and (at Warrington) to 9.46 and the earlier train calling at Frodsham at. 7.4,9 rather irksome.</p>
        <p>• Blackpool trains have been wailer sparingly dealt with, but there are none too many trains left. The 9.211 p.m. to Manoltester leaves at 9,51. rather alarming decision is that no trains .wili run on the low-level en Sundays, and those -desirous of enjoying the amenities of Thelwall and Lyn= will hive tO ge by road- Several trains on this line aro victims ef the new regime, 4i:eluding the 2.24 and 3.97 I. . No longer seed ono ask vriiether there is a war ea t bos.oecoe kes to as etddtatly—in glow-m/71*g %raise.</p>
