        <p>where his father, Mr. John Lowe, at present resides, came to Wttrrington about 'ten' years ago and took up his residence with his brother. He was employed as a lampman by the L. &amp; N.-W. Railway Company until September, 1914, when he enlisted, going to ' France about three months ago, On his 31st birthday. His wife, and child reside at. Southend. His. bro- ther, Leonard, is 9erving in India.</p>
