      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <head>MR. J. A. RANSOEVIE.</head>
        <p>MR. J. A. RANSOEVIE.</p>
        <p>NA hy He Resigned His Managing Directorship.</p>
        <p>Mr. J. A. Itaxisonie disclosed his reason for relinquishing the managing directorship of the Richmond, Gas Stove and .Meter Co., Ltd., when he presided at the annual dinner of the em- ployes. That was the first opportunity he had had .of being present on such an occasion, he said, and be was sorry to .say that it would also be his last. They had probably heard of his coming retirement from the position so Jong held, and he could assure them that it was no easy matter for him to give up such a position. It was, however, contrary to his principles to remain at the post he had so long occupied, and, conse- quently' be had decided to resign hip Position, and ;would leave the Arm at the end of the month. He hoped-to see the coMpany go ahead, ariil asked their employes to give it their loyal support. Mr. J. W. Slack, who ,was no stranger to 'them, had been appointed as his successor, and he would ask them to give him the same 'support that had been ertended to himself. The future of Richmond's would then be assured.. (Applause.)</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0093" n="art0093">
        <head>KINEMAS.</head>
        <p>THE KINEMAS.</p>
        <p>"Tom Brown's Schooldays" is now drawing crowded houses to the ever-popular Star Kinema,? Church-street.. Next week Phyllis Bedells, of the London Empire, in "Fairyland," and later Mary Pickford in " Hulds. of Holland," will,. it is certain, be popular with patrons of this house.</p>
        <p>_ At the Grand Electric Theatre, Bridge Foot, Charlie Chaplin as Don Jose in " Carmen " is proving a wonderful success. "Madam Butte- fly," .starring Mary Piekford, and " The Found- ling," and also ", Peg o' the Ring" should prove specially attractive 'during next week.</p>
        <p>That well-known "Matrimony," is now to be seen at the Pavilion, Sankey Green. Next veek,-"Two Men of Sandy Bar," featuring.ller- bort Boicworth, should prove attractive. "Annie Laurie," that far-famed film, is also to be -Shown next week. Starring Abna Taylor, this picture has been shown in the /eading hotKeo of the OsOlutry, a sofo'proof of is merit -</p>
      </div>
