        <p>POTSD"AAr VARIETY TROUPE</p>
        <p>Austin, Bothwell, Aston; Eaton, Buekley, Hurst and MeAvoy. Referee, Mr. J. Burgess.</p>
        <p>The visitors lost the toss and Hurst kicked of on a very heavy ground. They made the first attack. Eaton, tricking several opponents, centred nicely, and both Buckley and Hurst failed to accept a good opening. The home team were next prominent with a long attack on the visitor&amp; goal, which resulted in Hollins scoring theiA first goal., The Visitors re- sponded in confident style and in a few min- utes Hurst made the scores equal. Even, play followed to the interval without any further score. Half-time :—One goal each. On resuming, the visitors at once assumed the offensive, but were repulsed by the good defensive play of Hodkineon. After a spell of mid-field play the visitors returned to the attack, and after a brief reverse Hurst gained the lead by a good individual effort. The home team now increased their efforts and Fearns made a good attempt with a fast shot, but Walters Made a grand save. A few min- utes later the same player was more successful and made the scores.equal. There was' now a keen struggle for the lead and the visitors were handicapped_ by being short of a full team and the home team were better able to make the attack, and Hill scored a few min- utes before the final whistle .blew. Foams, Vodkinson, Hill and Murty played a good game for the home team, and the visitors were best represented by Hurst, Aston, Austin and Gibson. Result :—Widnes Juniors, 3 goals; Orford Juniors, 2 goals.</p>
        <p>and H. Bissell. Reserve, Harrison. Team to meet at Crosfield'a Recreation Ground at 2.15 prompt.</p>
