      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0141" n="art0141">
        <head>FRIENDLY MATCHES.</head>
        <p>FRIENDLY MATCHES.</p>
        <p>ST. MARY'S JUNIORS V. ST. JOHN'S JUNIORS.</p>
        <p>Played on Tuesday. St. John's won the toE..s. and played with the wind in tlipir favour! Challoner, after a fine run up the field, passed to Rothwell, who scored a good goal. A few minutes later Rose kicked through his own goal. St. Mary's then made an attack, and Stirrup scored their first goal. Half-time: St. John's, 2 goals; St. Mary's, 1 goal. Dolan equalised, and later a centre by Pugh \ended in a goal being scored by Rose. Rothwell then equalised for St. John's. Lee made a fine run up the field, but lost the ball when getting dangerous. Stirrup made a good run and passed to Rose, who allowed it to go in touch. From the throw-in Cox handled the ball in the penalty area, and Mannion scored a goi)-d goal. Before the game ended a goal was scored by each side. The pick of St. Mary's were Mannion, Dolan, Lee and Stirrup; and St. John's, Challoner, Rothwell, Cox and Cooke. Result: St. Mary's Juniors, 5 goals; St. John's Juniors, 4 goals.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-12-30_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <head>MATCHES FOR TO-DAY.</head>
        <p>MATCHES FOR TO-DAY.</p>
        <p>Orford Junior isv. Grappenhall; Mr. T. Smith. Bewsey A.S. v. Howley; Mr. W. Knight. Latchford Recs. v. Widnes Juniors; Mr. J. Wright. Widnes St. Mitry's v. S. Illphin's; Mr. J. Burgeee. Latchford Cadets T. Penketh; Mr. W. H. Hunter.</p>
        <p>TEAMS.</p>
        <p>ST. MARTS JUNIORS v. FAIRFIELD ROVERS.</p>
        <p>St. Mary's: J. McHugh; J. Mannion (eapt.), 11. Cullen ; A. Hill, J. Pugh, R. Kelly; J. Nola\l, A. Mtinup, J. Dolan, T. Lee and E. Kelly.</p>
        <p>' ST. ELPHIN'S v. WIDNES ST. MARY'S.</p>
        <p>On the Widnee County ground.</p>
        <p>St. Eiphin's: W. Povey ; H. Shelmerdine, V. Furness ; W. Watson, H. Miller (captain), 11. Gleave; H. Boyle, P. Hire, W. Lee, J. Willcoek and J. Holden. '</p>
        <p>• Players trarel by train, 1.8 Warrington Central.</p>
        <p>CROSFIELD'S ANIORS v. SANKEY RECS.</p>
        <p>At Hood-lane; kick-off 2.30. Crosfield's Team: S. Barton; A. Stanley, S. Ravenseroft; J. Jone, G. Appleton, A. Maeon; D. Morrison, H. Beswiek; S. Jres, W. Smith</p>
      </div>
