        <p>Notices of Births, Marriages, and Deaths, In Memori. Notices, and Acknowledgements of Syntathy are inserted in ' " The Examiner" at tho following rates:—Not exceeding 20 words, 1/6 each; every addi- tional seven words, Gd.</p>
        <p>Deaths. GIBSON..b—On Christmas Day. at 65, Manchester- road, Warrington. Alfred Gibson, aged 72 years. Interred at Warrington Cemetery on the 28th inst. ROLL OF HONOUR. WILSON.—In loving memory of our dear lad, Private Robert Wilson. K.0.5.8.'5, youngest son 4 of Daniel and Jane Wilson, of 246, Knuteford- road, Latchford, who was killed in action in Gallipoli on December 29th. 1915, aged 19 years. Loved by all who knew him. Be marched away so bravely. His head so proudly held, His footsteps never faltered, His c,ourags never failed. When on the field of battle He calmly took his place, And fought and died for Britain And the honour of his race. Had we but seen him yet in life, , Watched by his dying bed, Caught the last dickering of his breath, And touched his dying head, We think our hearte would not have felt Such bitterness of grief: But God hath willed it otherwise. _ And now he rests in Peace, in a soldier's grave.</p>
        <p>Acknowledgments. AirliS. ALFRED GIBSON and FAMILY wish ILL to THANK ell friends for kind sympathy ,a n d floral tributes in their sad bereavement. 65. Manchester-road. Warrington.</p>
