        <p>wife also having died. During his leave he resided . with Mrs. Maloney, 55, Lower Bank- street, where his child is now living. He was educated at King-street School, and was for- merly employed by Messrs. Rylands Bros., Ltd. His brother, Thomas, is in training with the Lancashire Fusiliers . PRIVATE W. H. LOWE. Former Railway Servant Killed By Sniper. Mr. Thomaq Lowe, Station House, Sankey Bridges, has received news that his • brother, Private Wilkiara Henry - Lowe, of the • Border Regiment, was. killed in action on November 300: According to a letter from an officer, Private Lowe was shot by a sniper while carry- ing a message and died instantly. "He was buried by his comrades a few hours after- wards," concluded the letter, "and a cross was erected to show where a faithful soldier lay." • • Private Lowe, who was 31 years of age, and a native of Kirkby Lonsdale, Westmorland,</p>
