        <p>PRIVATE R. BOND. Wcunded.</p>
        <p>PRIVATE F. S. BODEN. Killed Shortly After His Return To Duty. Official news reached Mr. and Mrs. H. Boden, 1, Fothergill-street, on Sunday, that their youngest son, Private Frederick Stanley Boden, of the Royal Warwickshire Regiment, was ;illed in action on December 10th. Mrs. Boden received a letter from her son, which had been posted on the =l9th inst., when he was quite well. Private Boden, who was 25 'years of age, only returned to the Front about three weeks ago, .after recovering from a wound sustained in</p>
        <p>PRIVATE F. .S. BODEN. Killed. ' August of this year. Whilst on leave at home he fell sick,' and spent about seven Weeks in the Lord Derby Hospital, Winwiek: An old boy" of the National School, and a former employe of Messrs. William Mortimer and Son, Orford Tannery, Private Boden enlisted: on the Ist September, 1914, and' went.to the Front in June of last year.: His brother, Abraham, is with the Royal Engineers in Egypt; while an- other, John; of the Royal Warwickshire'Regi.: merit, was discharged with frost-bitten feet after serving at the Dardanelles.</p>
